* cpu1: clearing the trip latch, and the latch letting go by itself.
*
* PG5 does not reach the latch's ~CLR. It reaches a 1 k resistor and a 4.7 nF
* capacitor, and the pull-up that holds ~CLR high is on the *far* side of that
* capacitor. `cpu1.py:1121` says why: a pin driven low and abandoned - an ISR
* spinning, a fault handler that still feeds the watchdog, a debugger halt -
* would otherwise hold the clear asserted for ever, and a held clear does not
* leave the board tripped. It leaves it oscillating: the comparator releases,
* the latch clears itself, PWM resumes, and it over-currents again.
*
* `test_the_clear_reaches_a_valid_low_and_lets_go_by_itself` computes this as
* three closed-form RCs. This runs it, and the reason that is worth doing is
* the **clamp**: D13 sits on the clear node with its cathode on the rail and
* it is the only nonlinear thing in the circuit. Without it the release
* overshoot is the rail plus what the capacitor is still holding - 6.61 V from
* this board's own declared values, against a latch whose absolute maximum is
* 6.5 and which has no clamp diode of its own, because that absence is what
* makes an LVC input 5 V tolerant. The check approximates the clamp as a
* capacitance. Here it is a diode with an I-V curve.
*
* **This is also the circuit that passed 203 checks with its capacitor set to
* zero.** The clamps were holding the node and nothing noticed, because every
* check was arithmetic that the clamps satisfied too. A deck cannot be fooled
* that way: take the capacitor out and there is no pulse to measure.
*
* Values come from the build; @path:end@ is an instance path and which end of
* its resolved range to take.

.include ../models/lvc1g74.lib
.include ../models/bat54a.lib

.param v3v3 = @rail.3v3.voltage:max@
V3v3 n3v3 0 DC {v3v3}

* --- the clear path ----------------------------------------------------------
*
* PG5: low at 10 us and **left there**, which is the abandoned-pin case, and
* released at 300 us so the overshoot the clamp exists for has somewhere to
* happen. An MCU pin drives to its own rail, so the high level is the rail.
Vpg5 pg5 0 PWL(0 {v3v3} 10u {v3v3} 10.001u 0 300u 0 300.001u {v3v3} 500u {v3v3})

Rseries pg5 couple @safety.r_clear_series.resistance:max@
Ccouple couple clr @safety.c_clear.capacitance:max@
Rpullup n3v3 clr @safety.r_clear_pullup.resistance:min@
Cclr clr 0 @copper.TRIP_CLEAR_LATCH_N.capacitance:nom@

* The clamp. Common anode on the clear node, one cathode on the rail and the
* other a no-connect, so what limits the release is one junction and the 1 k
* in front of it.
Dclamp clr n3v3 BAT54A

* --- the latch, so the clear is tested by what it is for ---------------------
*
* Preset first - something tripped - and then cleared, so this measures the
* latch coming out of a trip rather than a waveform on a node.
Vpre pre 0 PWL(0 {v3v3} 1u {v3v3} 1.001u 0 2u 0 2.001u {v3v3} 500u {v3v3})

Xlatch pre clr tripped trip_n n3v3 lvc1g74
+ tpre=@safety.latch.preset_to_output_max:max@
+ cref=@safety.latch.delay_load_reference:max@
+ vmeas=@safety.latch.delay_threshold:max@
+ ilim=@safety.latch.output_current_max:min@
+ vil=@safety.latch.input_low_voltage_max:max@
+ vih=@safety.latch.input_high_voltage_min:min@

Ctripped tripped 0 @copper.TRIPPED.capacitance:nom@
Rtripped n3v3 tripped @safety.r_tripped_pullup.resistance:min@
Ctrip_n trip_n 0 @copper.TRIP_N.capacitance:nom@
Rtrip_n trip_n 0 @safety.r_trip_n_pulldown.resistance:min@

.tran 2n 500u

* --- what happened -----------------------------------------------------------

* The low the clear reaches, which has to be a low the latch will act on.
.meas tran v_clr_low MIN v(clr) FROM=10u TO=300u

* How long it stays one. This is the number the whole arrangement exists to
* bound: the pin is still low at 300 us and this must have ended long before.
.meas tran tmp_clr_falls WHEN v(clr)=@safety.latch.input_low_voltage_max:max@ FALL=1
.meas tran tmp_clr_rises WHEN v(clr)=@safety.latch.input_low_voltage_max:max@ RISE=1
.meas tran t_clr_asserted PARAM='tmp_clr_rises - tmp_clr_falls'

* And that it really did let go, with the pin still held low: the node is back
* at the rail two hundred microseconds later and the pull-up owns it again.
.meas tran v_clr_released FIND v(clr) AT=290u

* The release, which is the clamp's whole job. Without D13 this is 6.61 V from
* this board's declared values against a 6.5 V absolute maximum on an input
* with no clamp of its own.
.meas tran v_clr_overshoot MAX v(clr) FROM=300u TO=400u

* And the thing it is all for: the latch coming out of the trip it was preset
* into.
.meas tran tmp_q_falls WHEN v(tripped)=@safety.latch.input_low_voltage_max:max@ FALL=1
.meas tran t_clear_to_q PARAM='tmp_q_falls - tmp_clr_falls'

.end
